# TypeScript Standards

## Strict Mode
- `strict: true` in tsconfig.json. No `any` types — use `unknown` and narrow.
- No `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error` without an adjacent comment explaining why.
- Enable `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`.
- Code must pass the **full CodeBuild typecheck**, not just compile in isolation. A local
  full-repo `tsc` hangs here — rely on CI for the authoritative check (see
  `cloud-first-verification.mdc`).
- A TS `interface` does **not** implicitly satisfy `Record<string, unknown>`; use a `type`
  alias (or add an index signature) when a value must be assignable to it (F-D8).

## Type Definitions
- Define domain types in `src/types/` (web) or `src/shared/types/` (api).
- One file per domain: `order.types.ts`, `customer.types.ts`, `catalog.types.ts`, `auth.types.ts`, `invoice.types.ts`.
- Export interfaces for object shapes, type aliases for unions/intersections.
- Use `z.infer<typeof schema>` to derive types from Zod schemas — never define the same shape twice.

## Imports
- Place imports at the top of the file. No inline imports in function bodies.
- Use path aliases: `@/components/`, `@/hooks/`, `@/lib/`, `@/types/`, `@/pages/`.
- Group imports: 1) React/external, 2) Internal modules (`@/`), 3) Relative imports, 4) Type-only imports.

## Naming
- `PascalCase` for components, types, interfaces, enums.
- `camelCase` for variables, functions, hooks (prefixed `use`).
- `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for constants and environment variables.
- Files: `kebab-case.ts` for utils, `PascalCase.tsx` for components.

## Error Handling
- Always type errors as `unknown` in catch blocks and narrow before accessing properties.
- Use custom error classes from `src/shared/errors/` (API) or `src/lib/errors.ts` (web).
- Never silently swallow errors — log + rethrow or return a meaningful error response.

## Exhaustive Switches
In switch statements over discriminated unions or enums, use a `never` check in the default case:

```typescript
function assertNever(x: never): never {
  throw new Error(`Unexpected value: ${x}`);
}
```
